commit 1941ac8d76059c9160ac21488819d8b93538b292
Author: ledger <ledger@example.invalid>
Date:   Mon Nov 23 01:58:20 2026 +0000

    Add a board for the committee's tasks
    
    Built from the task sheet export (incoming/tasks.csv, copied to boards/tasks/tasks.csv)
    with the existing kit, so it is kept up the same way as the events board.
    
    Sorted for what the minutes asked for: tasks with nobody's name first (water meter,
    shed gutter, ...), then overdue, then due by the next Thursday meeting, then later;
    done tasks folded at the bottom (Tomas). Cards, not a table, so no sideways scrolling
    on a phone (Hal). The polytunnel rota from the sheet's side columns is at the top, each
    week with its date, so it still reads right days after a rebuild (Dot).
    
    kit/board.py: a board.json with "due" instead of "section" builds a task board; columns
    may have "prefix" and "date"; status words match regardless of case (the export has
    "Done" next to "done"). The events board builds byte-identical to before.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

